        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ExcomVI">Excom VI</ref> 6</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Excom VI 6" corresp="#wit-ca"><pb n="436" ed="#liebermann"/>Maledictus sit equitando<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="p" target="#ExcomVI_6.lnote.oe.p"/> et non equitando. Maledictus sit manducando<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="q" target="#ExcomVI_6.lnote.oe.q"/> et bibendo. Maledictus sit cogitando et agendo. Maledictus sit operando<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="r" target="#ExcomVI_6.lnote.oe.r"/> et requiescendo. Maledictus sit dormiendo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="s" target="#ExcomVI_6.lnote.oe.s"/> et uigilando. Maledictus sit stando<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="t" target="#ExcomVI_6.lnote.oe.t"/> et sedendo. Maledictus sit ambulando<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="u" target="#ExcomVI_6.lnote.oe.u"/> et quiescendo.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 436 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
